    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5654\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing Steven Roy to file for retroactive membership in\nthe optional 20 year retirement plan of the New York state and local\npolice and fire retirement system pursuant to section 384-d of the\nretirement and social security law\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nProvides that officer Steven Roy may enter the 20 year retirement plan\nin the Town of Schodack.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one- Pursuant to section 384-d of the retirement and social\nsecurity law, the Town of Schodack has previously elected to offer the\noptional twenty year retirement plan to their police officer's.  The\nTown of Schodack is seeking to make such plan available to Steven Roy,\npolice officer, who, through no negligence of his own failed to apply\non time to participate in the retirement plan. Should the Town of\nSchodack elect to file with the state comptroller, on or before\nDecember 31, 2009, and the Schodack town board confirms, the above\npolice officer would be covered under the provisions of section 384-d\nand entitled to the full rights and benefits of the section should he\nrequest to do so with the state comptroller on or before June 30,\n2010.\n\nSection two- All past service costs associated with implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the town of Schodack.\n\nSection three- Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nSteven Roy, through no fault of his own failed to make a timely\napplication to participate in the optional twenty year retirement plan\nfor police officers in the Town of Schodack.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nThere will be no fiscal impact to the State. The Town of Schodack is\ngoing to pay the immediate past service cost of $20,500. Also, it will\nincrease the annual contribution of the Town of Schodack by\napproximately $2,500.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
